{"core": "Transformation ends what has finished and clears the ground for what comes next. Seated in its own position, that ending turns on itself: the very mechanism of letting go is what now needs to let go. When this goes unaddressed, the clearing never clears — old endings pile up, each one blocking the next thing from dying on time, and the ground stays occupied by what already left.", "sheetLine": "Old endings are stacking up; nothing new can finish."}
